    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0075" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.1012 Anti-War/80: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Argentine Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Saavedra Lamas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-30T19:00:00-04:00">April 30, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am particularly grateful for your felicitations and I reciprocate them since
                    Your Excellency rendered your efficacious cooperation towards a success which
                    will belong to all America when, after ratification by all the Parliaments, the
                    Anti-War Treaty will furnish us with the efficacious means of maintaining the
                    benefits of peace.</p>
                <p>Cordial greetings,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Saavedra Lamas</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
